==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|holy moly}}

===Etymology===
''c.'' 1892 as a euphemism for "Holy [[Mary]]", [[Molly]] being a nickname for Mary. Compare {{m|en|holy Moses}}.

===Interjection===
{{en-interj|head=[[holy]] moley!}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|dated|humorous or euphemistic}} {{non-gloss definition|An expression of [[surprise]]}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Running it off; or, Hard hit|author=Nathaniel Gould|year=1892|passage="Whew !" he whistled, softly; "that's curious. Same name as the lady at our place. Suppose he should be her husband. '''Holy moley''', what a game. I've made a discovery.|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=oDgPAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA217&dq=%22holy+moly|moley%22&hl=en&ei=m6k5Tq64DMfngQeG7aHPBg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CDIQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=%22holy%20moly|moley%22&f=false}}

